{#- Atlas — one milestone, and its plan (decisions 15, 18, 19).

  Markdown is the authority for content, so the plan renders as the file it already is. The
  manifest supplies only where the milestone stands.

  Two headings sit at the top of this page and that is correct: "Milestone 1 · Signal contract"
  is the manifest's own title spelled out as decision 19 requires, and the record's own heading
  below it is the file's, which decision 11 forces. They are different sentences from different
  authorities. (`document.njk` is the opposite case and prints only one.)

  Data this layout expects:
    workstream — the { slug, manifest } this milestone belongs to
    milestone  — one entry from that manifest's milestones
    planUrl    — the plan's own record page, so the reader can reach it as a record rather than
                 only as something inlined here
    recordUrl  — the acceptance record's page, or null when the manifest names none
    record     — the plan, already rendered by renderMarkdown. Not `content`: that is one of
                 Eleventy's reserved data names, and .eleventy.js keeps that guard switched on
    anchors    — headingAnchors(plan), for the contents list
    project, repo, title — see base.njk
-#}
{% extends "base.njk" %}
{% import "base.njk" as ui %}

{% block bodyClass %}page page-milestone{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Project depth</a> · <a href="{{ workstream.url }}">{{ workstream.manifest.codename }}</a></p>
{#- Decision 19: headings spell "Milestone 6.3" and the bare id is kept for chips and cells. The
    leading M comes off only when a number follows it, so a label that does not follow decision
    18's M<n> convention is printed whole rather than cut into. -#}
<h1>Milestone <span class="num">{{ milestone.label | replace(r/^M(?=\d)/, "") }}</span> · {{ milestone.title }} {{ ui.chip("status", milestone.status) }}</h1>

<ul class="meta-list">
<li><span class="meta-label">Recorded as</span><code>{{ milestone.id }}</code></li>
<li><span class="meta-label">Depth</span><span class="num">{{ milestone.depth }}</span></li>
<li><span class="meta-label">Acceptance</span>{{ milestone.acceptance.kind }}{% if recordUrl %} · <a href="{{ recordUrl }}"><code>{{ milestone.acceptance.record }}</code></a>{% elif milestone.acceptance.record %} · <code>{{ milestone.acceptance.record }}</code>{% endif %}</li>
<li><span class="meta-label">Plan</span><a href="{{ planUrl }}"><code>{{ milestone.plan }}</code></a></li>
<li><span class="meta-label">Issue</span>{% if milestone.issue %}<a class="num" href="https://github.com/{{ repo }}/issues/{{ milestone.issue }}">#{{ milestone.issue }}</a>{% else %}<span class="empty">None yet</span>{% endif %}</li>
<li><span class="meta-label">Pull request</span>{% if milestone.pr %}<a class="num" href="https://github.com/{{ repo }}/pull/{{ milestone.pr }}">#{{ milestone.pr }}</a>{% else %}<span class="empty">None yet</span>{% endif %}</li>
</ul>

{% if anchors | length %}
<nav class="contents" aria-label="Contents">
<span class="meta-label">In this plan</span>
<ul>
{% for heading in anchors %}
<li class="level-{{ heading.level }}"><a href="#{{ heading.id }}">{{ heading.text }}</a></li>
{% endfor %}
</ul>
</nav>
{% endif %}

<article class="doc">
{{ record | safe }}
</article>
{% endblock %}
